From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: program the TX DMA burst length and prefetch

The 64-bit DMA engine comes out of reset with 16-byte bursts and one
outstanding read; the TX control word reads back 0 at ring setup, so
keeping the reset values does not change that. On the BCM4360 (EA6900,
5 GHz VHT80, 3x3) the TX FIFO runs dry: the receiver sees about 4 MPDUs
per A-MPDU and the download stops at 118 Mbit/s at every channel width,
with the DMA ring nearly full.

Program the values Linux bgmac uses for the same DMA engine on Northstar
(128-byte bursts, 2 outstanding reads, prefetch 16, threshold 8). Measured
with firmware 784.2: 117 -> 326 Mbit/s TCP from the router, 118 -> 264
forwarded, 23 MPDUs per A-MPDU; 16 minute soak clean. TX only: the bgmac
RX values led to corrupted received frames (CCMP replay drops) within
minutes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
@@ -91,6 +91,10 @@
 #define		B43_DMA64_TXADDREXT_MASK		0x00030000
 #define		B43_DMA64_TXADDREXT_SHIFT		16
 #define		B43_DMA64_TXCTL_KEEP		0x03FC00C0	/* Outstanding reads, burst, prefetch */
+#define		B43_DMA64_TXMR_2			0x00000040	/* 2 outstanding reads */
+#define		B43_DMA64_TXBURST_128			0x000C0000	/* 128-byte bursts */
+#define		B43_DMA64_TXPREFETCH_16			0x00600000	/* Prefetch 16 descriptors */
+#define		B43_DMA64_TXPREFETCH_THRESH_8		0x03000000	/* Prefetch threshold 8 */
 #define B43_DMA64_TXINDEX				0x04
 #define B43_DMA64_TXRINGLO				0x08
 #define B43_DMA64_TXRINGHI				0x0C
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
@@ -717,6 +717,21 @@
 			enable = B43_DMA64_TXENABLE;
 			if (!parity)
 				enable |= B43_DMA64_TXPARITYDISABLE;
+			/*
+			 * The engine comes out of reset with 16-byte bursts and
+			 * one outstanding read (the control word reads back 0).
+			 * On the AC cores that cannot keep the TX FIFO fed at VHT
+			 * rates: the FIFO runs dry and the hardware cuts each
+			 * A-MPDU after about 4 frames (BCM4360, 5 GHz VHT80:
+			 * 118 Mbit/s at every width). Use the values bgmac
+			 * programs into the same DMA engine on Northstar. TX only:
+			 * the RX equivalents corrupted received frames.
+			 */
+			if (ring->dev->dev->core_rev >= 40)
+				enable |= B43_DMA64_TXMR_2 |
+					  B43_DMA64_TXBURST_128 |
+					  B43_DMA64_TXPREFETCH_16 |
+					  B43_DMA64_TXPREFETCH_THRESH_8;
 			if (ring->dev->dma.index_is_addr) {
 				value |= b43_dma_read(ring, B43_DMA64_TXCTL) &
 					 B43_DMA64_TXCTL_KEEP;
